# Drafted by Gemini (side quests batch 1: mare), edited.

~ start
Narrator: A broken halter dangles from the post, and the damp straw of the third stall is still warm.
marianna_grey [afraid]: The clocktower tolled and my grey mare Clover bolted straight up the northern moor road. Find her before the wolves do, and you will have my goodwill and three days free horse hire.
* We will find her -> accept
* Ask what Clover is like -> about
* Not now -> END

~ about
marianna_grey [neutral]: She is gentle as rain, just terribly skittish around flapping cloaks. Hold out a handful of dry oats and she will come right to your palm.
-> start

~ accept
marianna_grey [weary]: Mind the ditches out there. The fog hides the ruts, and she has got only one good shoe on her forelegs.
quest the_grey_mare asked
set mare_asked
-> END

~ progress
marianna_grey [weary]: Empty halter in my hand and wind rising off the heather. Have you seen a hide or hair of her yet?
* Any advice? -> advice
* [ends:the_grey_mare] We could not find her -> give_up
* Leave -> END

~ advice
marianna_grey [neutral]: Keep your cloaks tucked in and shake a pouch of oats if you get close. If the mud hides her prints, fetch Hilda Brom.
-> progress

~ give_up
marianna_grey [sad]: I see. Best I latch the third stall shut then, and save the clean straw for the horses that are left.
quest the_grey_mare lost
set mare_lost
standing patient_lady -1
-> END

~ tracks
Narrator: Deep, crescent hoofprints score the wet peat along the northern verge, filling slowly with black moor water.
* [Survival DC 12] Follow them -> tracks_ok | tracks_fail
* Ask Hilda Brom to track her instead -> tracks_hilda
* Leave -> END

~ tracks_ok
Narrator: Scuffed moss and snapped gorse stems mark a stumbling path toward a dark bramble thicket beside the north wall.
set mare_found
quest the_grey_mare found
-> END

~ tracks_fail
Narrator: The hoofprints vanish into a boggy churn of cart ruts and sheep droppings. Hilda Brom could read this mire better than you.
-> END

~ tracks_hilda
hilda_brom [neutral]: Thrown left shoe, panicked stride, dragging her halter rope through the gorse. Look in the thicket by the north wall.
set mare_found
quest the_grey_mare found
-> END

~ mare_there
Narrator: The dapple-grey mare stands tangled in wet briars by the stones, flanks heaving and ears pinned back at your shadow.
* [Animal Handling DC 12] Talk her down -> catch_ok | catch_fail
* Offer oats from the pack -> catch_oats
* [Athletics DC 14] Rope her -> catch_ok | catch_fail
* Leave her -> END

~ catch_ok
Narrator: Her trembling eases at your touch, and she lowers her velvet nose enough for {name} to take the frayed halter rope.
set mare_caught
quest the_grey_mare caught
-> END

~ catch_fail
Narrator: She snorts in terror, wrenching free of a briar to bolt a few yards down the wall. A handful of oats might steady her where quick hands failed.
-> END

~ catch_oats
Narrator: The dry grain rustles in your palm, and the mare steps out of the thorns to lip the oats from {name}'s fingers.
set mare_caught
quest the_grey_mare caught
-> END

~ return
Narrator: Clover presses her damp forehead against the stablemistress's shoulder, blowing a long, warm breath into her apron.
marianna_grey [smile]: Look at you, plastered in peat and burs, you foolish old girl. Take this coin for your trouble, friends, and any horse in my yard is yours free for three days.
set mare_returned
quest the_grey_mare done
gold +25
standing patient_lady +1
-> END
